Subject: [PATCH 02403/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE B3 (ARC
 NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17; breadth) -- E3 tr87 AND ft09 -> L1
 each, looped with a per-game checkpoint + hard per-game wall-time cap
 (breadth-of-progress beats an all-or-nothing single-game swing). Both are
 deep-tail games graph-explore NO-ADVANCEd; .401 (exp4329) reached partial
 models (ft09 ~0.10, tr87 ~0.00) BEFORE the explore-verify-plan upgrade that
 solved ar25/sc25. Apply the SAME upgraded harness (AERA explore-verify-plan
 arXiv:2605.25931 -- EXPLORE collects verifier-gated lemmas, PLAN only after
 mechanic checks; Agent2World adaptive world-model testing arXiv:2512.22336).
 The codex agent IS the proposer (WRITES results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py
 per game; NO nested CodexProposer). INCREMENTAL-PROGRESS scoped: +1 level
 (L1) EACH. HARD gate per game: offline_reproduced=true AND
 reproduced_levels>=1. An honest partial per game (best verifier_accuracy +
 the residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap) is PROGRESS.
 Report a per-game scorecard. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). NO
 TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH game so a
 window-exhaustion preserves the first game's result.

